+# Privacy implementation and third-party audit
+
+Reviewed October 28, 2026. Scope: both HTML pages, CSS, assets, package scripts,
+production server, and deployment headers in this repository.
+
+## Data minimization
+
+There are no forms, scripts, cookies, browser storage, analytics, advertising,
+fingerprinting, preconnects, or embedded services. Navigation links do not include
+personal data. Account/order/rewards routes are placeholders and return 404 here.
+The server accepts only GET and HEAD, uses an explicit public-file allowlist,
+does not log requests, and does not persist or reflect request data. Error messages
+do not disclose filesystem details. The build excludes source, configuration,
+and this audit from public output.
+
+## Third-party inventory
+
+| Component | Finding / action |
+| --- | --- |
+| Unsplash hero photograph | Previously requested remotely on each visit. Downloaded to `assets/coffee.jpg`; CSS now requests only this local asset. Source: https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1350&q=80 . |
+| Fonts | System fonts only; no remote font provider. |
+| Scripts and runtime packages | No third-party packages or browser scripts. Removed on-demand `pnpm dlx statikk`, which downloaded an unpinned server on startup. Production serving uses Node built-ins. Keep Node on a supported, patched release. |
+| Hosting/CDN/TLS provider | Deployment-specific; cannot be audited from this repository. Operator must document provider, subprocessors, location, access controls, and log retention before launch. |
+
+Repeat this inventory whenever an asset, dependency, embed, integration, or hosting
+provider changes. Review its purpose, transmitted fields, retention, subprocessors,
+and deletion capabilities. Prefer local assets. Obtain an explicit opt-in before
+any optional tracking starts, with an equally accessible withdrawal control.
+
+## Security headers and deployment
+
+Run `npm run build` to create the allowlisted `dist/` output. `npm start` builds
+and serves it using `scripts/serve.mjs`, which applies `_headers` to every handled
+response, including errors. It does not set cookies or log requests. Terminate TLS
+at a trusted HTTPS reverse proxy; this Node server uses HTTP behind that proxy.
+Redirect public HTTP to HTTPS at the edge. Do not expose the HTTP origin publicly.
+
+For static hosting, publish **only `dist/`**. Netlify and Cloudflare Pages support
+the included `_headers` format for static responses. Other hosts must configure
+equivalent response headers explicitly; copying the file alone is insufficient.
+Ensure proxies/CDNs retain the policy on errors and redirects, disable injected
+analytics, and check deployed response headers before launch.
+
+CSP disallows scripts, connections, forms, plugins, and framing, allowing only
+same-origin images/styles. HTML includes a fallback CSP and no-referrer metadata;
+`frame-ancestors`, HSTS, Permissions-Policy, and other response-only controls require
+the server headers. No inline style or script exceptions are needed. Responses use
+`no-store` to minimize retained browser/proxy data; this trades caching performance
+for privacy. HSTS is limited to this hostname; only enable subdomains/preloading
+after confirming their HTTPS readiness.
+
+## Secure handling for future services
+
+Before implementing accounts or ordering, define the minimum fields, purpose,
+retention/deletion schedule, and user access/export/deletion workflow. Do not put
+personal data, credentials, or tokens in URLs, HTML, analytics, or browser storage.
+Process validation and authorization on the server. Use HTTPS, encrypted storage,
+least-privilege access, redacted logs, and a managed payment processor for payments.
+Use Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite session cookies, session rotation, and CSRF protection
+for state changes (including logout); the existing logout link is a placeholder,
+not a working authenticated action. Relax CSP only for specific required origins
+and features after a privacy review. Never embed server secrets in public assets.
+
+The hosting operator must minimize/redact access logs and configure documented,
+short retention and restricted access. Do not claim that the hosting provider
+collects nothing: connection metadata is necessary to deliver pages. Keep the
+public privacy notice aligned with deployed behavior and actual provider policies.
+
+## Checks
+
+`npm test` verifies static privacy invariants and build publication boundaries.
+`node --check scripts/serve.mjs` checks server syntax without importing or starting
+it. These do not establish deployed proxy/TLS behavior or hosting log retention.
